= FAIR data — Simple =

FAIR data are data managed according to the FAIR Guiding Principles so that they are more Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable for people and machines.

FAIR emphasizes persistent identification, rich metadata, standardized access mechanisms, interoperable representations and vocabularies, provenance, licensing, and community standards.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* FAIR ≠ open
* FAIR ≠ data quality

